# The network of "Compare the two": the shop's server and its two DR sites,
# behind one private link.
#
#   shop 10.0.5.10 --- wan --- dr1 10.0.6.20   (50 Mbit/s, 1% loss)
#                          \-- dr2 10.0.7.20   (20 Mbit/s, no loss)
#
# wan is scenery: 25 ms each way to both sites (a 50 ms round trip). The
# link to dr1 carries 50 Mbit/s and loses 1% of the packets towards dr1 at
# random; the link to dr2 carries 20 Mbit/s and loses none.
machine shop
machine wan router
machine dr1
machine dr2

link shop:eth0=10.0.5.10/24 wan:shop=10.0.5.1/24
link wan:dr1=10.0.6.1/24 dr1:eth0=10.0.6.20/24
link wan:dr2=10.0.7.1/24 dr2:eth0=10.0.7.20/24

route shop default via 10.0.5.1
route dr1 default via 10.0.6.1
route dr2 default via 10.0.7.1

# Towards each site, where the data goes: its speed, its delay and (to dr1)
# its loss. Back towards shop, where the acknowledgements go, the delay only.
netem wan dr1 rate 50mbit delay 25ms loss 1% limit 2000
netem wan dr2 rate 20mbit delay 25ms limit 2000
netem wan shop delay 25ms limit 2000
